DATA

- NASA Open Science Data Repository, study OSD-575: "SpaceX Inspiration4 Blood
  Serum Metabolic Panel and Immune/Cardiac Cytokine Arrays" (data/mode2/).
  https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575
  NASA material, redistributed unchanged with this citation. The team has not
  yet verified the dataset's terms of use (see README.md).

- data/mode1/ (iss-synthetic-3000) is synthetic data generated by Ayman El Kerboubi for the team
  (Apache-2.0). Its
  column formats and value ranges follow these NASA sources:
  - Apollo 10 Mission Report, Table 10-I
    https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/a10-missionreport.pdf
  - Apollo-Soyuz Test Project report, Table 3-I
    https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19770023791/downloads/19770023791.pdf
  - Skylab experiment M171, Tables III-V
    https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19750006309/downloads/19750006309.pdf
  - NASA, "The Real Story About Astronaut Health Care in Space"
    https://www.nasa.gov/missions/station/faq-the-real-story-about-astronaut-health-care-in-space/
  - NASA OCHMO, "Exercise Overview" (OCHMO-TB-031)
    https://www.nasa.gov/ochmo-tb-031-exercise-overview-2/

- NASA Mars Science Laboratory (Curiosity) Radiation Assessment Detector,
  Level 2 observations, dataset MSL_RAD_OBS-L2, via NASA CDAWeb
  (data/radiation/). Exported to CSV by Ayman El Kerboubi;
  every reading keeps its NASA source file URL.
  https://data.nasa.gov/dataset/mars-science-laboratory-msl-radiation-assessment-detector-rad-level-2-observation-dosimetr
  Event context: NASA, "Curiosity Sees Streaks and Specks During 2024 Solar Storm"
  https://science.nasa.gov/resource/curiosity-sees-streaks-and-specks-during-2024-solar-storm/

